    {
      "id": "seg:code:overview:0009:0001",
      "blockId": "code:overview:0009",
      "type": "preserve",
      "source": "```swift\nclass Weather {\n    @Published var temperature: Double\n    init(temperature: Double) {\n        self.temperature = temperature\n    }\n}\n\nlet weather = Weather(temperature: 20)\ncancellable = weather.$temperature\n    .sink() {\n        print (\"Temperature now: \\($0)\")\n}\nweather.temperature = 25\n\n// Prints:\n// Temperature now: 20.0\n// Temperature now: 25.0\n```",
      "normalizedSource": "```swift class Weather { @Published var temperature: Double init(temperature: Double) { self.temperature = temperature } } let weather = Weather(temperature: 20) cancellable = weather.$temperature .sink() { print (\"Temperature now: \\($0)\") } weather.temperature = 25 // Prints: // Temperature now: 20.0 // Temperature now: 25.0 ```",
      "sourceHash": "c0a5d506da600ba911e120628fd55627214b4e2992c121c991ab4e6ce1258a89",
      "translatable": false,
      "preserveReason": "code",
      "contextBefore": "You access the publisher with the `$` operator, as shown here:",
      "contextAfter": "When the property changes, publishing occurs in the property’s `willSet` block, meaning subscribers receive the new value before it’s actually set on the property.",
      "documentTitle": "Published",
      "framework": "Combine",
      "ko": "```swift\nclass Weather {\n    @Published var temperature: Double\n    init(temperature: Double) {\n        self.temperature = temperature\n    }\n}\n\nlet weather = Weather(temperature: 20)\ncancellable = weather.$temperature\n    .sink() {\n        print (\"Temperature now: \\($0)\")\n}\nweather.temperature = 25\n\n// Prints:\n// Temperature now: 20.0\n// Temperature now: 25.0\n```",
      "status": "preserved",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": true
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:overview:0010:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:overview:0010",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "When the property changes, publishing occurs in the property’s `willSet` block, meaning subscribers receive the new value before it’s actually set on the property.",
      "normalizedSource": "When the property changes, publishing occurs in the property’s `willSet` block, meaning subscribers receive the new value before it’s actually set on the property.",
      "sourceHash": "3debc1461cc8903114891686ed1a2fc0613d63ab4a1495c4ba9ca398911464c5",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "```swift\nclass Weather {\n    @Published var temperature: Double\n    init(temperature: Double) {\n        self.temperature = temperature\n    }\n}\n\nlet weather = Weather(temperature: 20)\ncancellable = weather.$temperature\n    .sink() {\n        print (\"Temperature now: \\($0)\")\n}\nweather.temperature = 25\n\n// Prints:\n// Temperature now: 20.0\n// Temperature now: 25.0\n```",
      "contextAfter": "In the above example, the second time the sink executes its closure, it receives the parameter value `25`.",
